Theorem RL-11a: MaybeShared donor transfer depends on sharing observation

  Preconditions:
    - DP-6 admits the MaybeShared donor as a candidate.
    - A sharing observation yields one-owner or multiple-owner.

  Soundness property:
    Forall MaybeShared owned donor d and recipient r:
      (P1) one-owner permits donor-to-recipient owner-credit transfer.
      (P2) multiple-owner forbids transfer and requires an independent logical
           birth for r.
    The theorem does not select IsShared, a branch, Reset/Reuse, allocation, or
    storage mechanisms.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate both observation results.
    Coverage gate: 2 outcomes. Transfer on the multiple-owner result is the
    negative-direction witness and is rejected.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl11a_dynamic_reuse)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-11a admits owner-credit transfer only on the one-owner observation outcome and requires independent birth for multiple owners
